.\" Man page for the sciebo CLI.
.TH SCIEBO 1 "2026-09-24" "rclone-sciebo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sciebo \- synchronize local directories with a sciebo (Nextcloud/WebDAV) remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sciebo
.RI [ global\-options ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B sciebo help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B sciebo
.I command
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sciebo
synchronizes local directories with a sciebo (Nextcloud/WebDAV) account
through
.BR rclone (1).
Sources are declared in
.IR config/sources.conf ,
.IR config/folders.conf ,
and
.IR config/sources.generated.conf ;
each source is a pair of a local directory and a remote subdirectory below
.IR <RCLONE_REMOTE>:<REMOTE_BASE>/ .
.PP
Transfers and deletions happen only through
.B sciebo sync
and
.BR "sciebo cleanup \-\-apply" .
Every other command is read-only with respect to the remote unless its
description says otherwise. A failed command returns a non-zero status;
usage errors print the command usage to standard error.
.PP
Profiles provide independent accounts. Each profile keeps its own manifest,
filter, and state tree under
.I config/profiles/<name>/
and
.IR state/profiles/<name>/ .
Select one per run with the global
.B \-\-profile
option or by exporting
.BR SCIEBO_PROFILE .
The default profile is the project-wide layout.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options may appear before or after the command, but they are consumed
before the command runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Use the named profile.
.TP
.B \-\-trust
Accept invalid TLS certificates (rclone gets
.BR \-\-no\-check\-certificate ,
curl gets
.BR \-\-insecure ).
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Never prompt; fail or skip instead.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Verbose rclone and HTTP output.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " FILE"
Write the rclone log to
.IR FILE ;
.B \-
means standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-confdir " DIR"
Read configuration and state from
.IR DIR :
settings, manifests, filters, and the default state tree move below it.
The shipped
.I settings.env
stays the fallback when
.I DIR
has no settings file.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-dir " DIR"
Write run logs to
.I DIR
instead of
.IR <state>/logs .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-expire " HOURS"
Delete logs older than
.I HOURS
in
.BR "sciebo cleanup \-\-logs" ,
overriding
.BR LOG_RETENTION_DAYS .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the main usage text and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
Run
.B sciebo help
.I command
or
.IB command " \-\-help"
for the same usage text that documents the options below.
.SS "sciebo setup [\-\-login] [\-\-url URL] [\-\-no\-keychain] [\-\-rotate] [\-\-proxy URL] [\-\-crypt]"
Create or update the rclone remote named by
.B RCLONE_REMOTE
as a Nextcloud WebDAV backend and validate it.
.TP
.B \-\-login
Authenticate with the Nextcloud Login Flow v2, which opens a browser and
returns a fresh app password.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Base URL for
.BR \-\-login .
.TP
.B \-\-rotate
Fetch a fresh app password for the already-configured remote; cannot be
combined with
.B \-\-login
or
.BR \-\-url .
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " URL"
Use
.I URL
as the proxy for this setup run only; settings files are not written.
.TP
.B \-\-crypt
Create the crypt remote named by
.B CRYPT_REMOTE
(default
.IR <RCLONE_REMOTE>\-crypt )
wrapping the WebDAV remote with fresh randomly generated passwords; cannot
be combined with
.BR \-\-login ,
.BR \-\-rotate ,
or
.BR \-\-url .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-keychain
Store the obscured password in the rclone config for this run instead of the
macOS Keychain.
.SS "sciebo doctor [\-\-offline] [\-\-json]"
Run preflight checks and print PASS/WARN/FAIL lines plus a summary. Exits 1
if any check fails. The policy checks cover the active desktop-parity
settings: a compact
.B policies
line, local case-only clashes with
.BR CASE_CLASH_POLICY ,
end-to-end encrypted folders with
.BR E2EE_POLICY ,
mounted external storages with
.BR EXTERNAL_STORAGE_POLICY ,
the delete guard
.RB ( ASK_DELETE ,
.BR DELETE_FILES_THRESHOLD ,
.BR MAX_DELETE ),
and sources over
.B BIG_FOLDER_SIZE
with
.BR BIG_FOLDER_EXISTING_POLICY .
When
.B QUOTA_WARN_PERCENT
is above 0 it also reads the server quota once and reports WARN at or above
the threshold (PASS below, WARN when the probe fails; offline it reports the
threshold only).
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Skip network checks; the encrypted-folder, external-storage, and big-folder
scans report the policy only.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print only a JSON document instead of the text report. Besides
.B ok
and
.BR checks ,
the document carries the policy objects
.BR policies ,
.BR name_hygiene ,
.BR case_clashes ,
.BR e2ee ,
.BR external ,
.BR delete_guard ,
and
.BR big_folders .
.SS "sciebo discover [\-\-write]"
Scan the roots in
.I config/roots.conf
for git repositories and emit manifest lines.
.TP
.B \-\-write
Atomically write
.IR config/sources.generated.conf .
.SS "sciebo list [\-\-json]"
List the parsed sources with mode, name, local path, remote path, and filter,
including invalid entries with their error.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the valid entries as
.RB ( {"sources":[...]} )
with their origin (manual, folders, or generated); invalid lines keep going
to standard error.
.SS "sciebo check [options]"
Dry run of every source. Accepts the same options as
.BR "sciebo sync" ;
transfers stay disabled.
.SS "sciebo sync [options]"
Apply the sync, pull, and bisync entries of all configured sources.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Transfer data (default for
.BR sync ).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Explicit dry run (default for
.BR check ).
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Run only the entry whose sanitized name is
.IR NAME .
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the parsed sources (same as
.BR "sciebo list" )
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-resync
Allow
.B rclone bisync \-\-resync
(first-time initialization). A resync can copy or delete files in both
directions; review a dry run with
.B \-\-resync
first.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Download pull/bisync sources even when they exceed
.BR MAX_DOWNLOAD_SIZE ,
and disable the delete guard for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-metered\-ok
Run even when the connection is metered, overriding
.BR METERED_POLICY=skip
or
.B ask
for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Only print failures, warnings, and the final summary.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lock
Do not take the run lock.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Run even while paused (the global pause marker or a per-pair
.B folders pause
flag).
.PP
Desktop-parity policies apply per entry. With
.BR INVALID_NAME_POLICY=exclude
(the default) non-portable names are excluded; with
.BR CASE_CLASH_POLICY=exclude
(the default) the later name of a local case-only collision is excluded, and
.B rename
quarantines it as
.IR "<name> (case conflict)<ext>" .
.BR E2EE_POLICY=exclude
excludes end-to-end encrypted subfolders from pull/bisync and skips an entry
whose remote root is encrypted;
.BR EXTERNAL_STORAGE_POLICY=ask
asks once on a terminal before a remote root on mounted external storage;
.BR BIG_FOLDER_EXISTING_POLICY=warn
warns about configured sources over
.BR BIG_FOLDER_SIZE .
.BR MOVE_TO_TRASH=1
moves deleted or overwritten pull/bisync files into
.B LOCAL_TRASH_DIR
(default
.IR <state>/trash )
instead of deleting them;
.BR CHECKSUM=1
compares by checksum.
.B SYMLINK_POLICY
selects skip, follow, or translate. The upload chunk size is clamped to
.B MIN_CHUNK_SIZE
and
.BR MAX_CHUNK_SIZE ;
.B PROXY_TYPE
is validated and reported while the flags come from
.B PROXY
and
.BR PROXY_DIRECT .
.PP
The delete guard: with
.BR ASK_DELETE=1
(the default) and an unlimited
.BR MAX_DELETE ,
each apply passes
.B \-\-max\-delete
.BR DELETE_FILES_THRESHOLD .
When rclone stops because the threshold was reached, a terminal asks once to
continue without the cap; a non-interactive run fails the entry with a
message to re-run with
.BR \-\-yes .
An explicit
.B MAX_DELETE
of 0 or more overrides the guard.
.PP
With
.B QUOTA_WARN_PERCENT
above 0 the server quota is probed once before the entries (the same cached
probe
.B doctor
uses) and a
.B quota guard:
warning names the floor percentage used and the threshold. A probe error only
warns, and the check never fails a run.
.SS "sciebo verify [options]"
Check that every configured source matches its destination with
.BR "rclone check" .
Never transfers, deletes, writes logs, or takes the run lock.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Check only the source with this sanitized name.
.TP
.B \-\-download
Download remote files and hash them (slow; catches server-side corruption).
.TP
.B \-\-size\-only
Compare sizes only, skip hashes.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Only print failures and the summary.
.SS "sciebo status [options]"
Show the pause state and the last recorded run per configured source.
Read-only.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Show only the source with this sanitized name.
.TP
.BI \-\-history " [N]"
After each row, print its last N (default 10) recorded runs.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the pause state and one row per source as a single JSON document;
cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-watch .
.TP
.BI \-\-watch " [N]"
Refresh the report every N seconds (default 5) until interrupted with
INT/TERM.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Only print rows that need attention, plus the summary.
.SS "sciebo pause [\-\-for DURATION]"
Skip sync and check runs until
.BR "sciebo resume" .
Without
.B \-\-for
the pause is indefinite; an expired marker is removed automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-for " DURATION"
Pause for
.IR N [smhd]
(90m, 24h, 1d; a bare number means minutes).
.SS "sciebo resume"
Clear the pause marker so scheduled and manual runs continue.
.SS "sciebo folders [subcommand] [options]"
Choose sciebo folders to pair with local directories, Nextcloud-client
style. With no subcommand,
.B choose
runs. Only
.I config/folders.conf
and pair filter files under
.I config/filters/
are written; no data is transferred.
.TP
.B choose
Browse the remote and pick folders. Options:
.BR \-\-depth " N,"
.BR \-\-local\-root " DIR,"
.BR \-\-mode " MODE"
(sync, pull, or bisync),
.BR \-\-select ,
.BR \-\-no\-fzf ,
.BR \-\-no\-dry\-run .
Before a proposed pair is accepted,
.B BIG_FOLDER_POLICY
(default ask),
.B EXTERNAL_STORAGE_POLICY
(default ask), and
.B E2EE_POLICY
(default exclude) are applied in that order: ask confirms on a terminal and
skips otherwise, warn warns and proceeds, skip/exclude drop the pair, and
allow proceeds silently.
.TP
.BI "add \-\-remote " SUB " [options]"
Add a single pair without browsing; the remote subfolder is required.
Options:
.BR \-\-local " PATH,"
.BR \-\-mode " MODE,"
.BR \-\-select ,
.BR \-\-include " SUB"
(repeatable),
.BR \-\-exclude " SUB"
(repeatable),
.BR \-\-local\-root " DIR."
.TP
.B import FILE
Add a pair from a nextcloudcmd
.B \-\-unsyncedfolders
list (one remote-relative folder per line). Options:
.BR \-\-remote " SUB,"
.BR \-\-local " PATH,"
.BR \-\-mode " MODE,"
.BR \-\-local\-root " DIR,"
.BR \-\-select .
.TP
.BI "edit " "NAME [options]"
Rewrite a wizard-managed pair's local path, remote subfolder, filter, or
mode.
.I NAME
is the sanitized entry name from
.BR "folders list" .
At least one option is required. Options:
.BR \-\-local " PATH"
(replaces the local folder),
.BR \-\-remote " SUB"
(replaces the remote subfolder; an empty value or
.B /
means the remote base, stored as
.BR . ,
and the pair and its filter are renamed after the new remote),
.BR \-\-force
(allow a
.B \-\-remote
change even though initialized bisync state no longer matches the new path;
without it the change is refused, and the stale state is kept so a
.B "sync \-\-resync"
is needed),
.BR \-\-include " SUB"
(repeatable; every other immediate child is excluded),
.BR \-\-exclude " SUB"
(repeatable),
.BR \-\-mode " MODE,"
.BR \-\-select ,
.BR \-\-clear .
.TP
.B list [\-\-json]
Table of all configured pairs, including the per-pair
.B PAUSED
and
.B HIDDEN
flags; with
.B \-\-json
the same rows as
.RB ( {"pairs":[...]} )
plus boolean
.B paused
and
.B hidden
fields.
.TP
.BI pause " NAME"
Set the pair's per-pair paused flag so
.B sync
and
.B check
skip it (reported as skipped, not failed).
.I NAME
is the sanitized name from
.BR "folders list" .
The flag is stored as
.I paused=1
in a mode-600 file under
.B PAIR_FLAGS_DIR
(default
.IR <STATE_DIR>/pairs );
.B sync \-\-force
runs a paused pair anyway.
.TP
.BI resume " NAME"
Clear the pair's paused flag.
.TP
.BI remove " NAME [\-\-purge]"
Remove a wizard-managed pair from
.IR config/folders.conf .
.B \-\-purge
also deletes the pair's bisync workdir, run record, history file, blacklist
record, pair filter, and pair flag file; local data directories are never
touched.
.SS "sciebo mount [options]"
Mount the configured remote as a local filesystem with
.B rclone nfsmount
(no macFUSE needed). Mounts are created and removed only when the command is
run; nothing is scheduled automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " SUB"
Remote subfolder below the remote base.
.TP
.BI \-\-mountpoint " PATH"
Local mountpoint (default:
.B MOUNT_ROOT
or
.IR MOUNT_ROOT/<name> ).
.TP
.B \-\-ro
Read-only mount, no VFS cache.
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Run rclone in the foreground (Ctrl-C to unmount).
.TP
.B \-\-sudo
Run rclone as root; macOS NFS mounts usually need this.
.SS "sciebo umount ([\-\-folder SUB | \-\-mountpoint PATH | \-\-all]) [\-\-sudo]"
Unmount a recorded mount and remove its state.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " SUB"
Unmount the mount recorded for this remote subfolder.
.TP
.BI \-\-mountpoint " PATH"
Unmount the mount recorded for this local mountpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Unmount every recorded mount.
.TP
.B \-\-sudo
Run umount as root.
.SS "sciebo mounts [\-\-folder SUB] [\-\-check] [\-\-prune] [\-\-json]"
Show recorded mounts with mount visibility, rclone pid, and pid liveness.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " SUB"
Only show the mount recorded for this remote subfolder.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 1 when a recorded mount is not visible or its rclone is gone.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Remove state records for mounts whose mountpoint is not mounted and whose
pid is not alive.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the mounts as
.RB ( {"mounts":[{...}]} )
instead of the table; a pid is null when unknown.
.SS "sciebo cleanup (\-\-logs | \-\-uploads | \-\-state | \-\-junk | \-\-cache | \-\-support) [\-\-apply]"
Housekeeping for the tooling. Dry run by default: nothing is deleted unless
.B \-\-apply
is given. At least one of the category options is required. Refuses to run
while the local sync lock is held.
.TP
.B \-\-logs
Delete log files older than
.B LOG_RETENTION_DAYS
(or
.B LOG_EXPIRE_HOURS
when set) and rotate logs larger than
.B LOG_MAX_BYTES
to
.IR <file>.1 .
.TP
.B \-\-uploads
Delete stale chunk uploads under
.I /remote.php/dav/uploads/
older than
.BR CHUNK_CLEANUP_MIN_AGE .
.TP
.B \-\-state
Delete stale bisync workdirs, lock leftovers, atomic-write temp files, and
orphaned mount records older than
.BR STATE_CLEANUP_MIN_AGE .
.TP
.B \-\-junk
Delete files matching a glob in
.I config/filters/fleeting.txt
below every manifest source and older than
.BR JUNK_CLEANUP_MIN_AGE .
.TP
.B \-\-cache
Delete files under
.B MOUNT_CACHE_DIR
older than
.BR STATE_CLEANUP_MIN_AGE .
.TP
.B \-\-support
Keep the newest
.I support\-*.tar.gz
archives under
.B STATE_DIR
and delete the older ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep " N"
Archives to keep for
.B \-\-support
(default 5).
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually delete (default is a dry run).
.SS "sciebo logs [list] | show NAME [\-\-lines N] | tail NAME [\-\-lines N] | path [NAME]"
List, print, or follow the per-source sync logs in
.BR LOG_DIR .
Sources come from the manifest, the run records under
.IR state/last/ ,
and the per-source
.I *.log
files in
.BR LOG_DIR .
Read-only: no run lock, no state writes, and no network.
.TP
.B list [\-\-json]
Table of NAME, MODE, PATH, SIZE, MTIME, and the last recorded STATUS;
with
.B \-\-json
the same rows as
.RB ( {"logs":[...]} ).
.TP
.BI "show " NAME
Print the last
.B \-\-lines
lines (default 50) of NAME's log. The recorded last-run log is preferred,
otherwise the newest normal log, falling back to a dry-run log with a note
on standard error.
.TP
.BI "tail " NAME
Like
.BR show ,
but follow the file with
.BR "tail \-f" .
.TP
.B path [NAME]
Print the resolved log path as
.IR name<TAB>path ,
or one line per known source.
.TP
.BI \-\-lines " N"
Trailing lines printed by
.B show
and
.BR tail ;
a missing, zero, or non-numeric value is a usage error.
.TP
.B \-\-json
List as
.RB ( {"logs":[...]} ).
.PP
An unknown name exits 1 with the known names; a source without a log exits
1 for
.BR show ,
.BR tail ,
and
.BR path .
.SS "sciebo schedule install|uninstall|status"
Manage the per-user scheduler agent (launchd on macOS, systemd --user on
Linux) that runs
.B sciebo sync \-\-apply \-\-quiet
on the schedule configured in
.I config/settings.env
(daily at
.BR SCHEDULE_HOUR : SCHEDULE_MINUTE ,
every
.B SCHEDULE_INTERVAL
seconds, or when
.B SCHEDULE_WATCH_PATH
changes).
.B SCHEDULE_JITTER
adds a random delay before each run.
.TP
.B install
Render the unit(s) and start the agent/timer.
.TP
.B uninstall
Stop the agent/timer and remove the unit(s).
.TP
.B status
Show whether the agent/timer is installed and loaded.
.TP
.B \-\-at\-login
Install only: start the agent at login/boot, overriding
.BR SCHEDULE_AT_LOGIN .
.TP
.BI \-\-profiles " LIST"
Install only: render one extra agent per profile, labelled
.IR <LAUNCHD_LABEL>.<profile> ,
each running with
.BR \-\-profile
(comma or space separated).
.SS "sciebo trash [subcommand] [options]"
List or clean up the Nextcloud trashbin. The listing is read-only; IDs are
the last path segment printed by the listing.
.TP
.B list
List trashed items (default).
.TP
.B restore ID...
Restore items into their original location.
.B \-\-all
restores every listed item after one confirmation.
.TP
.B rm ID...
Permanently delete items. Asks once on a terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is given; a non-interactive run deletes them as before.
.TP
.B empty
Permanently delete the whole trashbin after one confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the
.BR restore \-\-all ,
.BR rm ,
or
.B empty
confirmation.
.SS "sciebo versions SUB [options]"
List the Nextcloud versions of a remote path below the remote base
(read-only by default).
.TP
.BI \-\-download " VERSION"
Save the version (default target
.IR ./<name>.<VERSION> ).
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Write the
.B \-\-download
body to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
Stream the
.B \-\-download
body to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-restore " VERSION"
Restore the version after confirmation.
.TP
.BI \-\-delete " VERSION"
Delete the version after confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the
.B \-\-restore
and
.B \-\-delete
confirmation.
.SS "sciebo share subcommand [options]"
Manage Nextcloud shares through the OCS sharing API.
.I SUB
is a remote path below the remote base; permissions are letters (r, w, d, c,
s) or a numeric mask. Link shares default to read-only (1), user and group
shares to all (31). The create subcommands
.RB ( link ,
.BR copy\-link ,
.BR user ,
.BR group ,
.BR email ,
.BR guest ,
.BR circle ,
.BR talk ,
.BR deck ,
.BR remote )
accept
.BR \-\-json :
they print
.RB ( {"id","type","url","permissions"} )
instead of the text line, omitting
.B url
when the server returned none;
.B copy\-link \-\-json
fails when the server returned no public link.
.TP
.BI "link " SUB
Create a public link share. Options:
.BR \-\-password " P,"
.BR \-\-expire " YYYY\-MM\-DD,"
.BR \-\-note " TEXT,"
.BR \-\-permissions " LETTERS,"
.BR \-\-label " LABEL,"
.BR \-\-download " 0|1"
(0 hides the download button; on Nextcloud 30+ this is the
.B attributes
array element, and the legacy
.RB ( {"download":0} )
object is used on older or unknown servers),
.B \-\-file\-drop
(upload-only link; unless
.B \-\-permissions
overrides it, this sets permission 4),
.B \-\-file\-request
(mark the link as a file request),
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BI "user " "SUB USER"
Share with a Nextcloud user. Options:
.BR \-\-permissions " LETTERS,"
.BR \-\-note " TEXT,"
.BR \-\-send\-mail .
.TP
.BI "group " "SUB GROUP"
Share with a Nextcloud group. Same options as
.BR user .
.TP
.BI "email " "SUB ADDRESS"
Share with an email address. Like
.BR user ,
plus
.BR \-\-password " P,"
.BR \-\-expire " DATE,"
.BR \-\-send\-mail ,
and
.B \-\-send\-password\-by\-talk
(password through Talk; needs
.BR \-\-password ).
.TP
.BI "guest " "SUB GUEST"
Share with a guest account (share type 8). Same options as
.BR user .
.TP
.BI "circle " "SUB CIRCLE_ID"
Share with a circle. Same options as
.BR user .
.TP
.BI "talk " "SUB ROOM_TOKEN"
Share with a Talk conversation. Same options as
.BR user .
.TP
.BI "deck " "SUB CARD_ID"
Share with a Deck board. Same options as
.BR user .
.TP
.BI "remote " "SUB [USER@]SERVER"
Share with a federated cloud id. Same options as
.BR user .
.TP
.BI "list [" SUB "] [\-\-reshares] [\-\-json]"
List shares, optionally only for
.IR SUB .
.B \-\-reshares
asks the server for reshares only, and
.B \-\-json
prints the rows as
.RB ( {"shares":[...]} ).
.TP
.BI "info " ID
Show one share.
.TP
.BI "update " ID
Change a share. Options:
.BR \-\-password " P"
or
.BR \-\-remove\-password ,
.BR \-\-expire " DATE"
or
.BR \-\-remove\-expire ,
.BR \-\-note " TEXT"
or
.BR \-\-remove\-note ,
.BR \-\-permissions " LETTERS,"
.BR \-\-label " LABEL,"
.BR \-\-download " 0|1,"
.B \-\-send\-mail .
.TP
.BI "remove " "ID [\-\-yes]"
Delete a share. Asks on a terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is given; a non-interactive run proceeds as before.
.TP
.BI "leave " "ID [\-\-yes]"
Leave a share shared with you. Asks on a terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is given; a non-interactive run proceeds as before.
.TP
.BI "pending [" "\-\-local|\-\-remote] [\-\-json]"
List shares waiting for your acceptance; the two selectors are mutually
exclusive and
.B \-\-json
prints
.RB ( {"pending":[...]} ).
.TP
.BI "accept " "ID [\-\-remote]"
Accept a pending share;
.B \-\-remote
forces the federated pending list.
.B "accept \-\-all [\-\-remote]"
accepts every pending share in the selected list(s) and cannot be combined
with an id.
.TP
.BI "decline " "ID [\-\-remote] [\-\-yes]"
Decline a pending share. Asks on a terminal unless
.B \-\-yes
is given, and a non-interactive run requires
.B \-\-yes
because a declined share can be lost.
.B "decline \-\-all [\-\-remote] [\-\-yes]"
declines every pending share in the selected list(s) after the same
confirmation, and cannot be combined with an id.
.TP
.BI "send\-email " ID
Ask the server to email an existing share to its recipient
.RB ( POST " /shares/{id}/send-email" ).
.TP
.B "remote\-list [\-\-json]"
List the accepted federated shares as an
.IR ID / Type / Owner / Target
table, or as
.RB ( {"remote_shares":[...]} )
with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BI "search " QUERY
Find sharees: users, groups, email, federated, circles, guests, and Talk
rooms (a server that rejects the extra types is retried with users and
groups only). Results are labelled with the sharee type.
.TP
.BI "copy\-link " SUB
Create or reuse a public link and copy it to the clipboard.
.TP
.BI "copy\-internal " SUB
Copy a direct internal link for
.IR SUB .
.TP
.B incoming [\-\-json]
List shares shared with you;
.B \-\-json
prints them as JSON.
.SS "sciebo notifications [options]"
List the Nextcloud notifications of the configured remote, newest first.
.B \-\-app
and
.B \-\-type
are exact, case-sensitive allowlists whose values are comma, space, or colon
separated; when they are absent the
.B NOTIFY_APPS
and
.B NOTIFY_TYPES
settings apply as defaults (empty means all).
.B \-\-limit
and the allowlists apply before
.B \-\-notify
sends anything.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Print and notify at most N notifications after filtering.
.TP
.BI \-\-app " LIST"
Only notifications from these apps.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " LIST"
Only notifications with these object types.
.TP
.B \-\-unseen
Only notifications not yet recorded in the seen cache; listing with
.B \-\-unseen
does not write the cache.
.TP
.BI \-\-action " ID LABEL"
Run the action labelled
.I LABEL
(case-insensitive) on notification
.IR ID ,
using the action's POST, DELETE, or PUT method. Cannot be combined with
.B \-\-delete
or
.BR \-\-delete\-all .
.TP
.BI \-\-delete " ID"
Delete one notification. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-delete\-all .
.TP
.B \-\-delete\-all
Delete every notification after confirmation; needs
.B \-\-yes
when not running interactively.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a desktop notification for each not-yet-seen notification.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the filtered notifications as one JSON document (with a
.B seen
flag per notification). Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-watch .
.TP
.BI \-\-watch " [N]"
Poll every N seconds (default
.BR NOTIFY_WATCH_INTERVAL ),
print and record new notifications, and continue until interrupted. Cannot
be combined with
.BR \-\-delete ,
.BR \-\-delete\-all ,
.BR \-\-action ,
or
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print no notification rows.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the
.B \-\-delete\-all
confirmation.
.SS "sciebo activity [options]"
Show the Nextcloud activity stream of the configured remote, newest first.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Print and notify at most N activities (default 20, maximum 100).
.TP
.BI \-\-since " DURATION"
Only activities newer than
.IR N [smhd]
(e.g. 90m, 24h, 7d; a bare number means minutes). Because the API cursor is
an activity id, the command walks it backwards in pages of 50 until a page
crosses the cutoff, the stream ends, or 10 pages were fetched; hitting that
cap warns that older entries were not fetched.
.B \-\-notify
is bounded by the same window.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a desktop notification for each not-yet-seen activity.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print no activity rows.
.SS "sciebo presence [show | set STATUS | clear]"
Show, set, or clear the Nextcloud user status. With no subcommand,
.B show
runs.
.B set
accepts online, away, dnd, or offline plus the options below.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
Publish a custom message.
.TP
.BI \-\-emoji " EMOJI"
Publish a status emoji.
.TP
.BI \-\-clear\-after " DUR"
Expire the message after
.IR N [smhd]
(a bare number means minutes;
.B \-\-clear\-after 0
clears the message).
.SS "sciebo lock SUB"
Lock a remote file below the remote base with a WebDAV LOCK carrying the
Nextcloud
.B X\-User\-Lock: 1
header. The lock token is recorded locally so
.B sciebo unlock
can release it.
.SS "sciebo unlock SUB"
Release a manual WebDAV lock on
.IR SUB .
The token is taken from the record written by
.BR "sciebo lock" ;
without one it is looked up on the server through PROPFIND.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Release every lock recorded under
.I state/remote-locks/
and drop the records whose UNLOCK succeeded (printing
.BR "unlocked PATH" );
confirms first and needs
.B \-\-yes
in a non-interactive run. Takes no
.IR SUB .
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the
.B \-\-all
confirmation. A record whose UNLOCK fails is warned about and kept.
.SS "sciebo locks [\-\-prune | \-\-unlock\-all] [\-\-yes]"
List the locks recorded by
.B sciebo lock
as NAME, PATH, and TOKEN.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Check every recorded path and forget records whose lock-token is gone.
.TP
.B \-\-unlock\-all
Release every recorded lock the same way as
.BR "unlock \-\-all" ;
asks for confirmation and needs
.B \-\-yes
in a non-interactive run.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the
.B \-\-unlock\-all
confirmation.
.SS "sciebo quota [\-\-json]"
Print the quota usage reported by
.B rclone about
.IR <remote> .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print rclone's JSON document instead of the plain table.
.SS "sciebo open [SUB] [\-\-print] [\-\-web]"
Open the local folder for
.IR SUB ;
the first manifest entry whose remote subdir, local path, or entry name
equals
.I SUB
wins. Without a match
.I SUB
is resolved below
.B FOLDERS_LOCAL_ROOT
(the root itself when
.I SUB
is omitted).
.TP
.B \-\-web
Open the Nextcloud Files app at
.I /<REMOTE_BASE>[/SUB]
in the browser instead of the local folder.
.TP
.B \-\-print
Print the resolved path or URL instead of opening it.
.SS "sciebo conflicts [options]"
Find local conflict files below every configured source. The scan is
read-only and purely local; two kinds are listed: conflict copies matching
.B CONFLICT_PATTERN
(default
.IR "conflicted copy" )
and case-clash quarantines renamed to
.IR "<name> (case conflict)<ext>" .
Remote-side case clashes are not detected here; run
.B sciebo sync \-\-dry\-run
to see them.
.TP
.BI \-\-resolve " MODE"
Resolve conflict files instead of listing them;
.I MODE
is
.BR keep\-local
(move the file over the original),
.BR keep\-remote
(delete the file, keeping the original),
.BR keep\-newest ,
.BR keep\-oldest ,
or
.B keep\-both
(rename the file to
.IR "<name> (local copy)<ext>" ).
Without
.B \-\-apply
this is a dry run.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Scan or resolve only the source with this sanitized name.
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " KIND"
Scan or resolve only one conflict kind:
.BR copy ,
.BR case ,
or
.B all
(default).
.TP
.B \-\-remote
List case clashes on the server (read-only) instead of local files. Cannot be
combined with
.BR \-\-resolve ,
.BR \-\-apply ,
.BR \-\-yes ,
or
.BR \-\-open .
.TP
.B \-\-open
List, then open each containing directory of a match once with the platform
opener. Read-only and unconfirmed; exits 0 and prints
.I no conflicts
when there is nothing to open. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-resolve ,
.BR \-\-apply ,
.BR \-\-yes ,
or
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Carry out the planned actions; destructive, so a terminal run asks once and
a non-interactive run needs
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the
.B \-\-apply
confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the resolve result as JSON (each item carries a
.B kind
field); requires
.BR \-\-resolve .
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print nothing; exit 1 when conflict files exist (except with
.BR \-\-open ).
.SS "sciebo retry [NAME [PATH]] [\-\-list] [\-\-all]"
Clear failure-blacklist entries so the next sync tries those paths again.
Without options,
.I NAME
clears every blacklisted path of that source;
.I NAME PATH
clears a single path.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Show all blacklist records and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Clear every source's records.
.SS "sciebo account list|add|import|remove|use|info|avatar|status"
Manage profiles, each an independent account with its own manifests,
filters, remote settings, and state.
.TP
.B list
Show every profile.
.TP
.BI "add " "NAME [\-\-remote R] [\-\-base B]"
Create a profile.
.TP
.B import [options]
Import accounts and folder pairs from the Nextcloud desktop client's
.IR nextcloud.cfg .
Options:
.BI \-\-nextcloud\-cfg " FILE"
(also the
.B NEXTCLOUD_CFG
environment variable; the defaults are the macOS app container, the macOS
legacy path, Linux, and
.IR %APPDATA%/Nextcloud/nextcloud.cfg ),
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
(select one account by 0-based index, user id, or target profile name; the
global
.B \-\-profile
flag is reused),
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-yes
(merge into an existing profile or manifest without asking), and
.BR \-\-json .
Account 0 becomes the default profile; other accounts become a profile named
after their user id when safe, else
.IR account<N> .
The
.B [General]
values with a sciebo equivalent map into the profile's
.IR settings.local.env ,
folder pairs are added as bisync pairs, and passwords are never imported:
run
.B setup \-\-login
or
.B setup \-\-rotate
for every imported profile afterwards. Without
.B \-\-yes
a terminal run asks once before merging into an existing profile; a
non-interactive run refuses (exit 2).
.TP
.BI "remove " "NAME [\-\-yes]"
Delete a profile's config and state.
.TP
.BI "use " NAME
Show how to activate a profile.
.TP
.B info [\-\-json]
Show the account on the server;
.B \-\-json
prints the info as JSON.
.TP
.BI "avatar [\-\-output " FILE "] [\-\-size " N "]"
Download the account avatar (default
.IR ./avatar\-<user>.png ,
size
.B AVATAR_SIZE
or 128).
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Show the remote, server, cache, and keychain state;
.B \-\-json
prints the same facts as JSON and still exits 1 when the server is
unreachable.
.SS "sciebo provision \-\-userid USER (\-\-apppassword PASS | \-\-apppassword\-fd N) \-\-serverurl URL [\-\-localdirpath PATH] [\-\-remotedirpath PATH] [\-\-isvfsenabled 0|1] [\-\-profile NAME]"
Create an account profile and configure its rclone remote without any
prompt, the way the desktop client's provisioning flags do. The rclone
remote is named after the profile; without
.B \-\-profile
the profile is
.IR provision\-<sanitized\ userid> .
Creating is create-or-update, so the command can be re-run. A folder pair
is only added when
.B \-\-localdirpath
is given; the pair is a regular two-way
.RB ( bisync )
sync, because there are no virtual files.
.TP
.BI \-\-userid " USER"
Nextcloud user id (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-apppassword " PASS"
App password (required unless
.B \-\-apppassword\-fd
is used; never printed). The value is visible in the process list.
.TP
.BI \-\-apppassword\-fd " N"
Read the app password from the already-open file descriptor N, keeping it out
of the process list.
.TP
.BI \-\-serverurl " URL"
Server base URL (required). A URL that already looks like a WebDAV path
fails; plain
.B http://
warns.
.TP
.BI \-\-localdirpath " PATH"
Local folder to pair (optional; without it only the account is created).
.TP
.BI \-\-remotedirpath " PATH"
Remote folder below the remote base (default
.IR / ,
the base itself).
.TP
.BI \-\-isvfsenabled " 0|1"
Desktop compatibility flag; 1 warns and is ignored, any other value is a
usage error.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Profile to create or update.
.PP
The pair is validated before anything is written. An existing source name
or remote folder in the profile fails rather than merging. The app password
goes to the platform keychain when
.B KEYCHAIN
is enabled, otherwise it is stored obscured in the rclone config. The
remote is validated with
.BR "rclone lsd" ;
a failed validation exits 1.
.SS "sciebo logout [\-\-revoke] [\-\-yes]"
Remove the rclone remote entry and both Keychain items for the active remote
(the plaintext
.IB <remote>#plain
slot and a legacy obscured slot). Manifests, state, and synced files are left
alone.
.TP
.B \-\-revoke
Revoke the app password on the server first with an OCS
.B DELETE
to
.IR /ocs/v2.php/core/apppassword .
The revoke runs before the local credentials are removed, so the stored secret
is still available; a failed revoke only warns and the local logout still
runs. Non-interactive runs need
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.SS "sciebo config list|get|check|edit"
Inspect the effective settings and where each value comes from. The layered
files
.RB ( config/settings.env ,
the environment,
.IR config/settings.local.env ,
and the active profile) are read without contacting a remote.
.TP
.B list [\-\-json] [\-\-all]
Print every setting as
.IR KEY=VALUE<TAB>source .
Without
.BR \-\-all ,
settings with an empty value are hidden. Credential-like values (password,
secret, token, apikey, proxy) print as REDACTED.
.TP
.B get KEY [\-\-json]
Print the effective value of one setting.
.TP
.B check [\-\-json]
Check the settings and required files as PASS/WARN/FAIL lines; exits 1 on
any FAIL.
.TP
.B edit
Create
.I config/settings.local.env
from the shipped example when missing and open it in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON (list, get, check).
.TP
.B \-\-all
List: also show settings whose value is empty.
.SS "sciebo support [\-\-output FILE] [\-\-no\-network] [\-\-json]"
Build a redacted debug archive for bug reports: the version banner, the
doctor report, redacted settings and rclone config, state listings, the
newest logs (last 200 lines each), capabilities, and the scheduler/mount
status. Passwords, secrets, tokens, and proxy values are replaced with
REDACTED; the doctor always runs offline.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Archive path (default
.IR state/support\-<YYYYmmdd\-HHMMSS>.tar.gz ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-network
Accepted for nextcloudcmd-style callers; the doctor is offline.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print
.RB ( {"archive":"...","files":N,"bytes":N} ).
.SS "sciebo nextcloudcmd [OPTIONS] SOURCEDIR NEXTCLOUDURL"
Run one two-way sync between
.I SOURCEDIR
and
.I NEXTCLOUDURL
with nextcloudcmd's option names. The WebDAV folder is
.IR <url>/remote.php/dav/files/<user>/<--path> ;
the first run initializes the rclone bisync state automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-path " SUB"
Remote folder below the user root.
.TP
.BI \-\-confdir " DIR"
Configuration base for this run (ignored when
.B SCIEBO_CONFDIR
is already set).
.TP
.BR \-\-user " USER, " \-u " USER"
User name.
.TP
.BR \-\-password " PASS, " \-p " PASS"
Password (an app password is recommended). The value is visible in the
process list; prefer
.BR \-\-password\-fd .
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-fd " N"
Read the password from the already-open file descriptor
.I N
instead, keeping it out of the process list. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-password .
.TP
.B \-n
Read credentials from
.IR ~/.netrc .
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Never prompt.
.TP
.BR \-\-silent ", " \-s
Errors only.
.TP
.B \-\-trust
Accept invalid TLS certificates.
.TP
.BI \-\-httpproxy " URL"
HTTP proxy URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " FILE"
Read exclude patterns from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-anchored " FILE"
Read patterns from
.I FILE
and anchor each at the sync root; blank lines and
.B #
comments are ignored and a missing file fails.
.TP
.BI \-\-unsyncedfolders " FILE"
Exclude every folder listed in
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-sync\-retries " N"
Retry the whole sync up to N times: after a successful run a dry-run probe
is repeated while it still reports remaining changes, and every following
full run counts toward N.
.TP
.BI \-\-uplimit " RATE"
Upload bandwidth cap (rclone size suffix).
.TP
.BI \-\-downlimit " RATE"
Download bandwidth cap.
.TP
.BR \-\-logdebug ", " \-\-verbose
Debug-level logging.
.TP
.BR \-\-progress ", " \-P
Show rclone's transfer progress. Terminal only, and suppressed by
.B \-\-silent
and by the internal
.B \-\-max\-sync\-retries
dry-run probe.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Sync hidden files (no
.B .*
exclusion).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report what would change, change nothing.
.SS "sciebo watch [options]"
Watch the local directories of the configured sources and run
.B sciebo sync \-\-apply \-\-quiet \-\-only NAME
when one changes. One watcher per profile is tracked in
.IR state/watch/ .
A source whose local directory is missing is skipped with a warning, and
runs are skipped while
.B sciebo pause
is active.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " N"
Poll interval and minimum seconds between two runs of the same source
(default
.BR WATCH_INTERVAL ).
.TP
.BI \-\-debounce " N"
Coalesce change events for N seconds (default
.BR WATCH_DEBOUNCE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-only " NAME"
Watch only this source; repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-interval " N"
Check the remote every N seconds and notify when it differs; 0 disables
(default
.BR WATCH_REMOTE_INTERVAL ).
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " BACKEND"
Change-detection backend:
.BR auto ,
.BR fswatch ,
.BR inotify ,
or
.BR poll
(default
.BR WATCH_BACKEND ).
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run one detection cycle, sync affected sources, exit.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Allow desktop notifications (overrides
.BR NOTIFY ).
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-no\-notify .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Disable desktop notifications even when
.BR NOTIFY=1 .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-notify .
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Only warnings and errors.
.SS "sciebo edit SUB [options]"
Download one remote file on demand, open it in an editor, and upload it
again when it changed.
.I SUB
is resolved through the manifest only: the first valid entry whose remote
subdir equals
.I SUB
or is a parent of
.I SUB
wins, and the local copy lives at that entry's local path. There is no
.B FOLDERS_LOCAL_ROOT
fallback, and
.I SUB
must name a file, not a directory. The run lock is held for the whole
operation.
.TP
.BI \-\-editor " CMD"
Editor command, possibly with arguments; the file path is appended last.
Without any editor the platform opener is used and the upload is skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-upload
Download and edit, but never upload.
.TP
.B \-\-lock
Take a WebDAV lock
.RB ( sciebo
.BR lock )
while editing and release it afterwards; a failed release only warns.
.PP
The editor is
.BR \-\-editor ,
then
.BR $EDITOR ,
then
.BR $VISUAL .
Change detection compares file modification time and size before and after
the editor exits; the command prints whether the file was uploaded,
unchanged, or (with
.BR \-\-no\-upload )
changed but not uploaded. A failed download, a missing or directory remote
path, an editor that removed the local file, and a failed upload exit 1.
.SS "sciebo limit [options]"
Cap rclone bandwidth for later
.B sciebo sync
runs. The limit is stored as a local marker (no server contact) and applies
until it expires or
.B sciebo unlimited
removes it. An active marker takes precedence over
.B BW_SCHEDULE
and
.BR BW_LIMIT_UP / BW_LIMIT_DOWN .
.TP
.BI \-\-up " RATE"
Upload cap (rclone size suffix, e.g. 2M;
.B off
lifts it).
.TP
.BI \-\-down " RATE"
Download cap (e.g. 5M).
.TP
.BI \-\-until " DUR"
Expire after
.IR N [smhd] ;
a bare number means minutes and 0 means no expiry (default).
.TP
.B \-\-show
Print the current limit without changing it.
.TP
.B \-\-clear
Remove the marker (same as
.BR "sciebo unlimited" ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the state as JSON.
At least one of
.BR \-\-up ,
.BR \-\-down ,
.BR \-\-until ,
.BR \-\-show ,
or
.B \-\-clear
is required.
.SS "sciebo unlimited"
Remove the bandwidth marker written by
.B sciebo limit
so later sync runs are uncapped again (unless
.B BW_SCHEDULE
or
.BR BW_LIMIT_UP / BW_LIMIT_DOWN
is configured). Prints
.IR unlimited .
.SS "sciebo network [\-\-json]"
Show the active network interface and Wi-Fi name, whether the connection is
metered (OS report,
.BR METERED_SSIDS ,
or a hotspot-looking SSID), the
.B METERED_POLICY
in effect, and the proxy mode for rclone and curl: the configured
.BR PROXY ,
.B direct
when
.BR PROXY_DIRECT=1 ,
or the environment.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the state as JSON.
.SS "sciebo filters sync|list|show|check"
Manage the rclone filter files in
.BR FILTER_DIR .
.B filters sync
replaces the cache and the generated server filter atomically and takes no
run lock.
.TP
.B sync [\-\-json]
Fetch the server's
.IR sync\-exclude.lst ,
cache the raw body, and regenerate the server filter file.
.TP
.B list [\-\-json]
Table of
.I *.txt
filter files plus the age and staleness of the server cache.
.TP
.BI "show " NAME
Print one filter file (bare file name).
.TP
.B check
Validate every
.I *.txt
filter with rclone's parser.
.SS "sciebo ignored [SUB] [options]"
List the local files that
.B sync
would not transfer. Each entry's local directory is listed twice, once
unfiltered and once with sync's filter layering, and the difference is
reported. The layering mirrors sync: the server-exclude filter, clutter and
pair filters, the conflict-pattern exclusion, hidden files, the
failure-blacklist excludes, and
.I .nosync
markers for sync/pull entries. Read-only: no run lock, no state writes, and
no remote contact.
.TP
.B SUB
Restrict the result to files under one local, local-relative, or
remote-relative path prefix.
.TP
.BI \-\-source " NAME"
Restrict the scan to one configured source; an unknown name exits 1.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print
.RB ( {"ignored":[{"source","local","path"}]} ).
.PP
A missing local directory is skipped with a warning and does not fail the
run; an
.B rclone lsf
failure for one entry warns and the command exits 1.
.SS "sciebo file subcommand [options]"
Show details for a remote path below
.IR <RCLONE_REMOTE>:<REMOTE_BASE>/ .
.TP
.B info SUB [\-\-json]
Show WebDAV metadata for
.IR SUB .
.TP
.B activity SUB [\-\-limit N] [\-\-json]
Show the activity stream of
.IR SUB ;
.B \-\-limit
defaults to
.BR FILE_ACTIVITY_LIMIT .
.TP
.B shares SUB [\-\-json]
List the shares of
.IR SUB
(same as
.BR "share list SUB" );
.B \-\-json
forwards to
.BR "share list SUB \-\-json" .
.SS "sciebo search TERM [\-\-limit N] [\-\-json] [\-\-open]"
Search files on the server with Nextcloud's unified search.
.I TERM
is a single argument (quote it to search for spaces). Results are printed
as
.IR TITLE<TAB>SUBLINE<TAB>RESOURCEURL ,
or
.IR "no matches" .
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Ask the server for at most N results (default
.BR SEARCH_LIMIT ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the results as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the first result with the platform opener.
.SS "sciebo recent [\-\-since DUR] [\-\-limit N] [\-\-json]"
List recently modified files below
.IR <RCLONE_REMOTE>:<REMOTE_BASE>/ ,
newest first, as
.IR MODIFIED<TAB>SIZE<TAB>PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-since " DURATION"
Only files modified within
.IR N [smhd]
(e.g. 90m, 24h, 7d).
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Print at most N files (default
.BR RECENT_LIMIT ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the files as JSON.
.SS "sciebo comments SUB [list] | SUB add MESSAGE | SUB delete ID"
List, add, or delete comments on the remote path
.I SUB
below
.IR <RCLONE_REMOTE>:<REMOTE_BASE>/
(Nextcloud comments app).
.B list
is the default and prints the comment id, actor, creation time, verb, and
message.
.TP
.B SUB [list] [\-\-json]
List the comments of
.IR SUB .
.TP
.BI "SUB add " MESSAGE
Post a new comment.
.TP
.BI "SUB delete " "ID [\-\-yes]"
Delete one comment after confirmation; needs
.B \-\-yes
when not running interactively.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
List at most
.I N
comments (default: the
.B COMMENTS_LIMIT
setting, 50).
.SS "sciebo favorites [list] | add SUB | remove SUB"
List the server-side favorites of the configured remote, or mark
.I SUB
as a favorite.
.B list
is the default and prints the path, size, and last-modified time.
.TP
.B [list] [\-\-json]
List the favorites.
.TP
.BI "add " SUB
Mark
.I SUB
as a favorite.
.TP
.BI "remove " SUB
Clear the favorite flag of
.IR SUB .
.SS "sciebo tags list|create|assign|clear"
Manage Nextcloud system tags.
.TP
.B [list] [\-\-json]
List the id, display name, and the user-visible/user-assignable flags.
.TP
.BI "create " NAME
Create a user-visible, user-assignable tag.
.TP
.BI "assign " "SUB ID[,ID...]"
Replace the tags of
.I SUB
with a comma-separated id list.
.TP
.BI "clear " SUB
Remove every tag from
.IR SUB .
.SS "sciebo server info|capabilities|status"
Inspect the configured Nextcloud server or check that it answers.
.TP
.B info [\-\-json]
Server URL, user, and capability facts.
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-raw]
Parsed capabilities summary;
.B \-\-raw
prints the cached raw OCS response.
.TP
.B status
Reachability check with
.B rclone lsd
(PASS/FAIL).
.SS "sciebo hydrate SUB [options]"
Download a remote path below the remote base on demand.
.I SUB
is copied with the same filter layering as sync: the server-exclude filter
(when
.BR FILTER_SERVER_SYNC=1 ),
.IR clutter.txt ,
the matching manifest entry's filter file, the conflict-pattern exclusion
(unless
.BR CONFLICT_UPLOAD=1 ),
hidden files (when
.BR SKIP_HIDDEN=1 ),
the failure-blacklist excludes, and
.I .nosync
markers. The destination is the local directory of the first manifest entry
whose remote subdir equals
.I SUB
or is a parent of
.IR SUB ,
with the remaining relative path appended; without a match it is
.IR FOLDERS_LOCAL_ROOT/SUB .
With
.B \-\-dest
the contents of
.I SUB
are copied into the given directory instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-dest " DIR"
Copy the contents of
.I SUB
into
.I DIR
instead of the resolved destination.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report what would be copied; changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Do not print the success line.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print
.RB ( {"path","dest","dry_run"} )
instead of the text line.
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Show rclone's transfer progress
.RB ( \-P ).
Terminal only, and suppressed by
.B \-\-quiet
and
.BR \-\-json .
.SS "sciebo announcements [options]"
List the Nextcloud announcements of the configured server, newest first
(the announcementcenter app must be installed and enabled; when it is
absent or disabled the command prints
.B "announcements app not available"
and exits 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Print at most
.I N
announcements (default 20, max 100).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dismiss
Accepted for compatibility; announcements are not dismissed yet.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the announcements as a JSON document.
.SS "sciebo preview SUB [options]"
Download a preview image of the remote file
.I SUB
below the configured remote base.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
Write the image to
.I FILE
(default
.BR DEFAULT_PREVIEW_FILE ,
.IR ./preview );
.B \-
writes to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " N"
Preview edge size in pixels (default
.BR PREVIEW_SIZE ,
256).
.SS "sciebo download SUB [DEST] [options]"
Download a remote file or directory below
.IR <RCLONE_REMOTE>:<REMOTE_BASE>/ .
A single file is fetched over WebDAV to
.I DEST
(default: the basename under the current directory, or below
.B DOWNLOAD_DIR
when set); a directory is copied with rclone using the same filter layering
as
.BR "sciebo hydrate" .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report what would be transferred; change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Download even when the destination already matches the remote size.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Continue a partial destination with a range request (alias
.BR \-\-continue ).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Do not print the success line.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a structured summary.
.TP
.B \-\-progress
Show rclone's transfer progress
.RB ( \-P )
for rclone transfers. Terminal only, and suppressed by
.B \-\-quiet
and
.BR \-\-json .
.SS "sciebo update [--check] [--json]"
Update the local checkout from its git upstream. With
.B \-\-check
the upstream is fetched and the local revision compared with it without
changing the working tree; a source tarball or a branch without an upstream
is reported and exits 0. Without
.B \-\-check
the checkout is updated with
.BR "git pull \-\-ff\-only" .
The user's configuration is never modified.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Only report the local vs upstream state.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the report as JSON.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config/settings.env
Shipped default settings. Override values in
.I config/settings.local.env
(not committed) or in the environment instead of editing this file.
.TP
.B config/settings.local.env
Local setting overrides; plain assignments win over the environment.
.TP
.B config/sources.conf
Manual source manifest; one
.I mode | local_path | remote_subdir [| filter_file]
line per source.
.TP
.B config/folders.conf
Wizard-managed folder pairs in the same format; written by
.BR "sciebo folders choose" ,
.BR add ,
and
.BR import .
.TP
.B config/sources.generated.conf
Manifest generated by
.BR "sciebo discover \-\-write" .
.TP
.B config/roots.conf
Roots scanned by
.BR "sciebo discover" .
.TP
.B config/filters/
rclone filter files referenced by manifest entries, plus
.IR clutter.txt ,
.IR fleeting.txt ,
and the generated
.I server\-exclude.txt
(written by
.BR "sciebo filters sync" ).
.TP
.B config/profiles/<name>/
Per-profile settings, manifests, and filters.
.TP
.B state/
Run state: logs (
.IR logs/ ),
run locks (
.IR locks/ ),
bisync workdirs (
.IR bisync/ ),
mount records (
.IR mounts/ ),
mount cache (
.IR mount-cache/ ),
last-run records (
.IR last/ ),
failure blacklists (
.IR blacklist/ ),
history (
.IR history/ ),
remote lock records (
.IR remote-locks/ ),
seen markers (
.IR notifications\-seen ,
.IR activity\-seen ),
the pause marker (
.IR paused ),
the watch pid records (
.IR watch/ ),
the bandwidth marker (
.IR bwlimit ),
cached server sync-exclude list (
.IR sync\-exclude.lst ),
support archives (
.IR support\-*.tar.gz ),
and cached capabilities (
.IR capabilities.env ,
.IR capabilities.json ).
.TP
.B state/profiles/<name>/
Per-profile state with the same layout.
.TP
.B ${RCLONE_CONFIG} (default ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf)
rclone configuration written by
.BR "sciebo setup" .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure, including failing checks, failed transfers, and
conflict copies found by
.BR "sciebo conflicts \-\-quiet" .
.TP
.B 2
Usage error; the command usage text is printed to standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCIEBO_PROFILE
Active profile; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-profile
option.
.TP
.B RCLONE_REMOTE
Name of the rclone remote (default
.BR sciebo ).
.TP
.B KEYCHAIN
Store the plaintext app password in the platform keychain
.RB ( KEYCHAIN=1 ,
account
.IR <remote>#plain )
instead of the obscured value in the rclone config. A legacy obscured keychain
item is migrated once; with
.B KEYCHAIN=0
the obscured value stays in the rclone config and is still revealed with
.BR "rclone reveal" .
.TP
.B TLS_INSECURE
Accept invalid TLS certificates; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-trust
option.
.TP
.B CLIENT_CERT
PEM client certificate for mutual TLS
.RB ( rclone " \-\-client\-cert,"
curl
.BR \-\-cert );
must be a readable file when set.
.TP
.B CLIENT_KEY
PEM private key for
.BR CLIENT_CERT
.RB ( rclone " \-\-client\-key,"
curl
.BR \-\-key ).
.TP
.B CLIENT_KEY_PASSWORD
Plaintext passphrase for an encrypted
.BR CLIENT_KEY ;
rclone receives it obscured
.RB ( \-\-client\-pass ),
curl through a mode-600
.B \-\-config
file so it stays out of the argv.
.TP
.B CA_CERT
PEM CA bundle used instead of the system trust store
.RB ( rclone " \-\-ca\-cert,"
curl
.BR \-\-cacert ).
.TP
.B USER_AGENT
Override the HTTP User-Agent
.RB ( rclone " \-\-user\-agent,"
curl
.BR \-A ).
.TP
.B SCIEBO_NON_INTERACTIVE
Never prompt; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-non\-interactive
option.
.TP
.B SCIEBO_DEBUG
Verbose rclone and HTTP output; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-debug
option.
.TP
.B SCIEBO_LOG_FILE
Path of the rclone log, or
.B \-
for standard output; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-log\-file
option.
.TP
.B SCIEBO_CONFDIR
Configuration and state base; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-confdir
option.
.TP
.B SCIEBO_LOG_DIR
Directory for run logs; equivalent to the global
.B \-\-log\-dir
option.
.TP
.B SCIEBO_LOG_EXPIRE_HOURS
Delete logs older than this many hours in
.BR "sciebo cleanup \-\-logs" ;
equivalent to the global
.B \-\-log\-expire
option.
.PP
The nextcloudcmd and desktop-client
.B OWNCLOUD_*
variables are accepted as aliases when the matching setting is not
exported directly:
.BR OWNCLOUD_CHUNK_SIZE " (CHUNK_SIZE),"
.BR OWNCLOUD_TIMEOUT " (TIMEOUT, seconds),"
.BR OWNCLOUD_MAX_PARALLEL " (MAX_PARALLEL_SOURCES),"
.BR OWNCLOUD_CRITICAL_FREE_SPACE_BYTES " (MIN_FREE_SPACE),"
.BR OWNCLOUD_FREE_SPACE_BYTES " (FREE_SPACE_DOWNLOAD),"
.BR OWNCLOUD_BLACKLIST_TIME_MIN
and
.BR OWNCLOUD_BLACKLIST_TIME_MAX " (BLACKLIST_TIME_MIN/MAX),"
.BR OWNCLOUD_UPLOAD_CONFLICT_FILES " (CONFLICT_UPLOAD),"
and
.BR OWNCLOUD_HTTP2_ENABLED " (HTTP2_ENABLED)."
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR rclone (1)
.PP
The project README documents the manifest format, the settings precedence,
and the full configuration reference:
.I README.md
in the rclone-sciebo project tree.
